cations, such as applications that require immediate responses, as the method may introduce additional latency.\nPractical Considerations:"), mdx("p", null, "Training Data: The quality and quantity of training data will significantly impact the performance of ECPT.\nComputational Resources: ECPT requires significant computational resources, including GPU acceleration and large amounts of memory.\nIntegration with Existing Systems: ECPT needs to be integrated with existing systems, which can be time-consuming and require significant development effort.\nIn conclusion, ECPT has the potential to be a useful method in practice, particularly in scenarios where accuracy and efficiency are critical. However, its adoption will depend on various factors, including the quality of training data, computational resources, and integration with existing systems."), mdx("h4", {
