  }))), "Experience using the LLM"), mdx("p", null, "My process for using the LLM - Llama Scout 4 was interactive, I provided the full research paper and then asked it the given set of questions by giving it prompts slightly modified with the hope of getting better more specific responses that are not off track.\nI gave it prompts asking about the summary, motivation, results, limitations and such. For each question the LLM generated a paragraph level that restated the contributions of the paper.\nOverall, the LLM performed consistently and reasonably well. It produced clear and coherent summaries and explanations that aligned with the paper's idea. For example it did identify the paper proposes ECPT pipeline which was inspired by the medical diagnosis treatment process and was supported by RAG and embedding fine tuning.\nI felt the LLM was good at rephrasing the paper's ideas in a comprehensive language. It was good to extract and understand the major concept of the paper as it was able to answer all the questions asked. Another important thing it acheived was it was able to maintain consistency across all the questions, showing it could keep track of the paper's\ncore contributions and could keep referncing back to it while giving its answers. "), mdx("p", null, "Overall, I would say the LLM was helpful for getting an overall high level quick summary of the paper."), mdx("h4", {
